# Copy to .env and edit. Every value has a working default: with this file
# absent entirely, the system runs on SQLite + hashing embeddings + the stub
# client, which is why `make run` works on a clean checkout with no services.
#
# Each variable below *overrides* an automatic choice. Leave one unset and the
# system picks based on what is installed and configured (see app/config.py).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model access
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set this and the Anthropic client is selected automatically. Unset, the
# deterministic stub runs instead -- the whole pipeline still works, and the
# eval harness scores it, which is what makes the stub a baseline rather than
# a mock.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

# Force a backend regardless of the above: anthropic | stub
# LLM_BACKEND=stub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set DATABASE_URL and pgvector is used, with row-level security enforcing the
# group filter a second time inside the database. Unset, SQLite is used and
# the same filter is applied as a SQL predicate.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://invoice:invoice@localhost:5432/invoice_check
# STORE_BACKEND=sqlite
# SQLITE_PATH=var/chunks.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Retrieval
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# sbert | hashing   (sbert is chosen automatically if sentence-transformers is
# installed; hashing is a dependency-free fallback, much weaker semantically)
# EMBEDDING_BACKEND=hashing
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2

# cross-encoder | lexical   (lexical is BM25 over the candidate set)
# RERANKER_BACKEND=lexical
# RERANKER_MODEL=cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2

# Stage 1 fetches CANDIDATE_K by vector similarity; stage 2 reranks and keeps
# RERANK_K. Raising CANDIDATE_K costs recall-time only; raising RERANK_K puts
# more (and weaker) clauses in front of the model.
# CANDIDATE_K=20
# RERANK_K=4

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Decision thresholds -- these tune the false-flag/false-match trade directly
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Below this confidence, a line with plausible alternative clauses is called
# ambiguous and sent to a human rather than decided. Raise it to catch more
# genuine ambiguity at the cost of more manual review.
# AMBIGUITY_THRESHOLD=0.75

# Hard stop for the tool-calling loop.
# MAX_AGENT_ITERATIONS=6

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paths
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA_DIR=data
# VAR_DIR=var
# TRACE_PATH=var/traces.jsonl
